// Title: Lace Tempest Cobalt Strike Download
// Sigma ID: aa5b0a40-ed88-46aa-9fdc-0337b379ca9d
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-11-09 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects specific command line execution used by Lace Tempest to download Cobalt Strike as
//   reported by SysAid Team
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://www.sysaid.com/blog/service-desk/on-premise-software-security-vulnerability-notification
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-emerging-threats/2023/TA/Lace-Tempest/proc_creation_win_apt_lace_tempest_cobalt_strike_download.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "-nop -w hidden -c IEX ((new-object net.webclient).downloadstring(" and ProcessCommandLine contains "/a')"
